From: muOS R35S port
Subject: [PATCH] power: rk817_battery: clear the off counter once read

OFF_CNT (0x6F, minutes the PMIC was off) is set at a power-up, but a warm
reboot keeps the previous value. On 2026-11-17 every reboot read
off=141min, so the BSP's OCV calibration ran on each warm reboot with the
OCV register, which is also only sampled at a power-up: 3880 mV (69%)
replaced a counted 57% and patch 0002 then moved the display to it (+12
points after a reboot). Patch 0005's stale-OCV check (30 points against
the voltage estimate) did not catch it. Clear OFF_CNT after reading it at
boot, so a warm reboot reads 0 (no OCV calibration) and a real power-off
counts from 0. Logged as "muos-gauge: off count N min (now M)"; M != 0
means the register is read-only and another fix is needed.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
---
--- a/drivers/power/rk817_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/rk817_battery.c
@@ -1793,6 +1793,16 @@
 {
 	battery->is_first_power_on = is_rk817_bat_first_pwron(battery);
 	battery->pwroff_min = rk817_bat_get_off_count(battery);
+	/* muOS R35S port: the PMIC sets OFF_CNT (minutes off) at a power-up
+	 * but a warm reboot keeps the old value: on 2026-11-17 every reboot
+	 * read off=141min, so the BSP recalibrated to the OCV register, which
+	 * is only sampled at a power-up too (3880 mV, 69%, against a counted
+	 * 57%: +12 points after a reboot). Clear it once read, so a warm
+	 * reboot reads 0 and keeps the counted SOC. */
+	if (battery->pwroff_min)
+		rk817_bat_field_write(battery, OFF_CNT, 0);
+	BAT_INFO("muos-gauge: off count %d min (now %d)\n", battery->pwroff_min,
+		 rk817_bat_get_off_count(battery));
 	battery->pwron_voltage = rk817_bat_get_pwron_voltage(battery);
 
 	DBG("%s, is_first_power_on = %d, pwroff_min = %d, pwron_voltage = %d\n",
